
🌻

Usage instructions for the Unison Codebase Manager
You are running version: <VERSION>

To get started just run unison

Use unison [command] --help to show help for a command.

Usage: unison [-v|--version] 
              [(-c|--codebase CODEBASE/PATH) | 
                (-C|--codebase-create CODEBASE/PATH)] [--exit] [--lsp-format] 
              [COMMAND | [--token STRING] [--host STRING] [--port NUMBER] 
                [--allow-cors-host STRING] [--ui DIR] 
                [-p|--project project/branch] [--no-file-watch]]

Available options:
  -h,--help                Show this help text
  -v,--version             Show version
  -c,--codebase CODEBASE/PATH
                           The path to an existing codebase
  -C,--codebase-create CODEBASE/PATH
                           The path to a new or existing codebase (one will be
                           created if there isn't one)
  --exit                   Exit repl after the command.
  --lsp-format             [Experimental] Enable formatting of source files via
                           LSP.
  --token STRING           API auth token
  --host STRING            Codebase server host
  --port NUMBER            Codebase server port
  --allow-cors-host STRING Host that should be allowed to access api (cors)
  --ui DIR                 Path to codebase ui root
  -p,--project project/branch
                           Launch the UCM session at the provided project and
                           branch.
  --no-file-watch          If set, ucm will not respond to changes in unison
                           files. Instead, you can use the 'load' command.

Available commands:
  version                  Print the version of unison you're running
  mcp                      Run the MCP server using stdin/stdout
  init                     This command has been removed. Use --codebase-create
                           instead to create a codebase in the specified
                           directory when starting the UCM.
  run                      Execute a definition from the codebase, passing on
                           the provided arguments. To pass flags to your
                           program, use `run <symbol> -- --my-flag`
  run.compiled             Execute a definition from a previously compiled file,
                           passing on the provided arguments. To pass flags to
                           your program, use `run <file> -- --my-flag`
  run.file                 Execute a definition from a file, passing on the
                           provided arguments. To pass flags to your program,
                           use `run.file <file> -- --my-flag`
  run.pipe                 Execute a definition from stdin, passing on the
                           provided arguments. To pass flags to your program,
                           use `run -- --my-flag`
  transcript               Execute transcript markdown files
  transcript.fork          Execute transcript markdown files in a sandboxed
                           codebase
  transcript.in-place      Execute transcript markdown files on the specified
                           (or default) codebase
  headless                 Runs the codebase server without the command-line
                           interface.
